      "writtenOn": "2022-05-13T03:49:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack for the headers.\n\nI changed the implementation because vendors were never allowed to load the policy themselves. There is a selinux rule specifically for that: http://cs/android/system/sepolicy/public/domain.te;l\u003d417;rcl\u003dc7ca014555b411986cae6d9174a28a782a318f24\n(before that (ag/883592), this rule was `neverallow { domain -init } kernel:security load_policy`, which has the same effect). So if a vendor calls this function, `security_load_policy` will fail and the functions will effectively return -1. The only differences are: log messages are different and there is an access to a file. But surely these are side-effects and not part of the API?",
      "parentUuid": "c2cc8a00_e2afb865",
      "revId": "3b215b5573cb89de8f7811497eeaddf989572ab7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
